{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "PhysicsColumn",
  "description": "Full-physics column subassembly of the EqWeather reference suite (WRF em_scm_xy with ra_lw_physics = ra_sw_physics = 1, sf_sfclay_physics = 1, bl_pbl_physics = 1; cu = shcu = fdda = 0), i.e. everything WRF's first RK step does to a column except the land-surface scheme and microphysics: the RRTM longwave chain (components/atmospheric_radiation/rrtm_lw, five stages), the Dudhia shortwave scheme (components/atmospheric_radiation/dudhia_sw), the revised MM5 surface layer (components/atmospheric_dynamics/sfclayrev) and the YSU boundary layer (components/atmospheric_dynamics/ysu), mounted by reference as top-level systems and coupled in the WRF call order with variable_map/param_to_var edges (esm-spec 10.4): radiation -> rthraten -> YSU (cloud-top entrainment branch), surface layer -> u*, fm, fh, Ri_b, wind speed, 10 m wind, z0 -> YSU, and the assembly's shared scalar state into every scheme. The exposed rth_phys_sum = rthraten + dtheta/dt|PBL is WRF's RTHRATEN + RTHBLTEN. The column state enters each scheme through its input_<x> rewrite targets via template libraries injected at the mount edges (esm-spec 9.7.10; all from the same WRF step), so one document holds one regime. NOT co-mounted: the slab land-surface scheme (PLAN.md gap (n): document-scoped index sets forbid a 4-layer and a 59-layer column on the same axis) -- its fluxes are prescribed (hfx_lsm, qfx_lsm); and WSM6 (an in-place step in WRF's microphysics_driver, no condensate tendencies in this SCM regime). KNOWN BINDING LIMITATIONS (Rust CLI, EarthSciAST issue #198): the mounted components' own inline tests are re-run inside this document under the coupling and error, so run `./esm test --model PhysicsColumn <this file>`; the leaves' index sets are redeclared at document level because a top-level ref mount does not merge them; a parent test cannot set a mounted component's parameter, so the shared scalars are prescribed in this model and coupled in. Measured implicit-vs-instantaneous PBL tendency gaps at this regime (Linf, zero-tolerance run): dtheta/dt 1.94e-6 K/s (rthblten max 1.57e-4, 1.2 %), du/dt 1.48e-5 m/s^2 (rublten max 3.6e-4), dv/dt 3.50e-6 m/s^2, dqv/dt 5.3e-10 1/s (rqvblten max 6.5e-8); tolerances 3e-6, 2e-5, 2e-5, 1e-9 -- the stable nocturnal layer is far less stiff than the daytime one, so the implicit-explicit gap is 10x smaller. All other residuals (zero-tolerance run): surface-layer outputs <= 4.9e-5 relative (the real32 kernel's own floor vs its real64 replay is 5.3e-5), h 3.3e-5 relative, K_h/K_m Linf <= 8.2e-5 m^2/s, longwave fluxes Linf <= 2.0e-4 W/m^2, dthdt_lw 4.4e-9 K/s, dthdt_sw 0 K/s, gsw 1.8e-6, glw 3e-7, olr 1.7e-7 relative.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "eqweather",
   "assembly",
   "coupling",
   "radiation",
   "rrtm",
   "dudhia",
   "surface-layer",
   "pbl",
   "column"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Skamarock, W. C., et al. (2021). A Description of the Advanced Research WRF Model Version 4.3. NCAR Tech. Note NCAR/TN-556+STR."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
  },
  "NBUF": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 44,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of buffer layers MM5ATM adds above the model top, nint(p_top / (100 deltap)) with deltap = 4 hPa (RRTMINIT: NLAYERS = kme + nint(p_top*0.01/deltap) - 1); 44 for the reference column (p_top = 177.6 hPa)."
  },
  "NGPT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 140,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of g-points after the 256-to-140 reduction."
  },
  "NBANDS": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 16,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of longwave bands."
  },
  "PLANCK_T0": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 159,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. TOTPLNK(i, band) holds the band Planck integral at T = PLANCK_T0 + i kelvin, i = 1..181 (RRTM's INDLEV = INT(T - 159.))."
  },
  "PLANCK_NODES": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 181,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Temperature nodes of the TOTPLNK table (160..340 K)."
  }
 },
