   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_step300_physics_column",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay_physics=1 (sfclayrev) sf_surface_physics=1 (slab) bl_pbl_physics=1 (YSU), data/eqwefic/scm_ref) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork: at the PHYSICS-DRIVER level (commit 592f693, module_esm_dump hooks around radiation_driver, surface_driver + pbl_driver and the physics-tendency sum in dyn_em/module_first_rk_step_part1.F; dumps subassembly_rad/_pbl/_all at step 300, column its of row jps) and at the KERNEL level for the same step (sfclayrev scm_ref_600.json, RRTM scm_ref2_600.json with the in-kernel internals, Dudhia scm_ref_600.json). All references are real32 model values, so the contract is rel 1e-5 (CLAUDE.md), widened where documented. This document runs the WHOLE column physics of the step except the land-surface scheme: RRTM longwave (RRTMColumn -> RRTMSetcoef -> RRTMGasOptics -> RTRNSweep -> RRTMLWHeating) and Dudhia shortwave give rthraten = dthdt_lw + dthdt_sw; the revised MM5 surface layer (SfclayRev) gives u*, fm, fh, Ri_b, wind speed, 10 m wind and z0; YSU receives those and rthraten and gives the boundary-layer tendencies; every stage is fed through variable_map/param_to_var edges into `<x>_in` coupling-target parameters (the mount-edge libraries lower the components' `input_<x>` rewrite targets to them), and only the column state of the step, the surface scalars and the slab's fluxes are prescribed. Tolerances: surface-layer fluxes and profile functions rel 5e-05 and the Ri_b-derived stability quantities (psim, psih, br, rmol, flhc) rel 1e-04 (1e-6 where exact) -- the references are the real32 model's own outputs, and at this regime the real32 kernel differs from its real64 replay by up to 5.3e-5 (rmol, psim; the stable regime amplifies real32 roundoff in theta_v1 - theta_vs through the bulk Richardson number), so unlike the components' own tests (real64 references, rel 2e-5) the assembly tolerances follow the real32 floor; PBL height rel 5e-05 (the surface layer's residuals propagate into YSU's bulk-Richardson height search: measured 3.3e-5), kpbl and regime exact, K_h/K_m Linf abs 5e-3 m^2/s (real32 dump), longwave fluxes Linf abs 5e-3 W/m^2 and dthdt_lw/rthraten Linf abs 2e-8 K/s (the RRTM end-to-end contract: the sweep consumes the gas optics' quantised ITR, exact up to +/-1 flips), dthdt_sw Linf 1e-9 K/s (binary64 roundoff), gsw/glw/olr rel 2e-5. The PBL TENDENCIES and rth_phys_sum are asserted only LOOSELY: WRF's rthblten/rublten/rvblten/rqvblten are the IMPLICIT tridiagonal step's (c_new - c_old)/dt at dt = 60 s while the assembly evaluates the instantaneous right-hand side (PLAN.md 0.3); the tolerances (3e-06 K/s for dtheta/dt and rth_phys_sum, 2e-05 m/s^2 for du/dt and dv/dt, 1e-09 1/s for dqv/dt) sit above the measured implicit-explicit gaps of this regime (given in the model description) and document that gap rather than test the physics -- the physics is pinned by the components' own small-dt tests; a stage-3 comparison at the WRF step must apply the same implicit step to the assembled tendencies. The slab land-surface scheme is NOT co-mounted (its 4-layer soil column shares the column_nonuniform_1d axis lev at a different size and esm index sets are document-scoped, PLAN.md gap (n)), so the fluxes YSU receives are the slab's driver-level values prescribed as hfx_lsm/qfx_lsm, while sfc_hfx/sfc_qfx are the surface layer's own values checked against the kernel dump; the driver-level th2/t2/q2 are overwritten by the land-surface branch of surface_driver, so those three are referenced to the kernel-level sfclayrev dump. Regime: step 300 (00:00 UTC = 17:34 LST, sunset, coszen < 0 so gsw = 0 and dthdt_sw = 0), stable land column: slab hfx = -19.1 W/m^2 (sfclayrev's own -19.13), Ri_b = 0.058 (regime 1), u* = 0.208 m/s, h = 556 m, kpbl = 10, thin cirrus (qi <= 1.7e-6), glw = 264, olr = 239 W/m^2.",
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "psfc0": 97132.9453125,
      "tsk0": 281.521240234375,
      "xland0": 1.0,
      "mavail0": 0.6000000238418579,
      "pblh_prev0": 560.720947265625,
